---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import BubongTool from "../components/BubongTool.astro";
---
<Base title="ghost-watts · what can your roof do?" pathname="/bubong">
  <section class="max-w-prose mx-auto px-6 pt-12 pb-2">
    <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-ink-500 mb-3 font-mono">ghost-watts &middot; your roof, from space</p>
    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl mb-4 leading-tight">Can I install solar on my roof?</h1>
    <p class="text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      Drop your address. You'll get a yes-or-no verdict, the actual savings number for your bill, and what your block's existing solar density means for the engineering review. We measure your roof from satellite and look up the 617 rooftop solar installations our computer-vision survey already detected across Greater Metro Manila — all in your browser, nothing about your address leaves it.
    </p>
  </section>

  <BubongTool />

  <section class="max-w-prose mx-auto px-6 py-8 text-xs text-ink-500 leading-relaxed border-t border-ink-300/30 mt-12">
    <p class="mb-2"><strong>How it works:</strong> we geocode your address (Photon, Komoot's free OSM-backed service), find your building's outline (OSM building footprints via Overpass), measure its rooftop area, pull a hi-res satellite tile of it (Esri World Imagery), and run the solar payback math against the latest Meralco residential rate (₱12.50/kWh) and a PH-average yield from PVGIS (~1315 kWh/kWp/year).</p>
    <p>The neighborhood context and LGU permit data come from the ghost-watts pipeline: a custom computer-vision model trained on labeled rooftop solar from public mapping data, then run across 45,752 high-resolution satellite tiles spanning NCR plus adjacent Bulacan, Cavite, Rizal, and Laguna LGUs. Calibrated to 96% precision on a never-trained validation set. Methodology and caveats: <a href="/methodology" class="text-accent-steel no-underline">/methodology</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
